# DTF tier manifest: scan-on-proxy-coordinate-pins  (artifact-keeper 1.12.0:
# #4952, epic #4097)
# Profile-set: filesystem + the mock-scan-formats upstream. LOCAL-ONLY: the
# verdicts come from the backend image's bundled Grype and its pre-seeded
# vulnerability DB (no scanner sidecar, no OSV, no internet).
#
# WHAT IT GUARDS: the 1.12.0 Go, Composer and Conan gates (#4103, #4105,
# #4108) first graded a proxied archive only on what it bundles, so the
# requested coordinate's own advisories were never looked up: a module zip
# of golang.org/x/text v0.3.0, a dist of guzzlehttp/guzzle 6.5.0 or a Conan
# archive of openssl/1.1.1k with nothing vulnerable inside read `clean`.
# #4952 pins the request coordinate in the scan workspace (a go.mod require,
# a composer.lock, a conan.lock), so each is 403 scan_blocked, and a clean
# archive is graded with the pin cataloged (components_cataloged >= 1).
#
# Red: ak-backend:1.11.5 (none of the three formats is gated). Green: an image
# carrying artifact-keeper#4952.
PROFILES="storage.filesystem upstreams.mock-scan-formats"
